.\"
.\" NANOSLEEP(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH NANOSLEEP 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
nanosleep \- high-resolution sleep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <time.h>
.PP
.BI "int nanosleep(const struct timespec *" req ", struct timespec *" rem ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR nanosleep ()
suspends the execution of the calling thread until either at least
the time specified in
.I req
has elapsed, or the delivery of a signal that triggers the invocation
of a handler in the calling thread or that terminates the process.
.PP
If the call is interrupted by a signal handler,
.BR nanosleep ()
returns \-1, sets
.I errno
to
.BR EINTR ,
and writes the remaining time into the structure pointed to by
.I rem
(unless
.I rem
is NULL).
.SS The timespec structure
.nf
struct timespec {
    time_t tv_sec;   /* Seconds (64-bit on Substrate) */
    long   tv_nsec;  /* Nanoseconds [0, 999999999] */
};
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned.
.PP
On error or interruption, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINTR
The call was interrupted by a signal.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I tv_nsec
is out of range.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 162
Arguments:      req, rem (on stack)
.fi
.SS Resolution
The actual sleep resolution depends on the kernel timer tick rate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sleep (3),
.BR usleep (3),
.BR clock_gettime (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
